IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`

-- g7-art21-23-expressions: Part 6, Articles 21 to 23: the prohibition of unauthorized use of the expressions "registered by the Commissioner", "charity" and "Jersey charity"; the excepted foreign charity;
-- and the offences with their penalties as data.
--
-- Shape.  Each prohibition is a regulative rule (SHANT) typed by who is bound and what is done, with the facts that make it bite as the condition in front of it; the same facts also answer a plain
-- BOOLEAN ("the statement contravenes paragraph (n)") so that the offence and the penalty can be read off.  No SHANT carries a WITHIN: the Law states no period, and a borrowed deadline would let the
-- prohibition lapse (phrasebook 5.3).  A discretion is an input: "knows, suspects or has reasonable grounds to suspect", "intends", the meaning of "in connection with any of its activities in Jersey"
-- and whether an exception prescribed by the States by Regulations applies are facts the caller supplies; the content of the Regulations and of the Order under Article 22(2)(a)(ii) is an input.
-- The entity's standing comes in on the standard names of integration points IP5, IP6 and IP26: `the entity` (a Jersey entity, or not), `the entity is a registered charity`, and
-- `the entity is an excepted foreign charity` (which Article 22 below computes).
--
-- Forks.  F7.4: the strict offence of paragraph (1) (or (3), (5), Article 23(1)) and the knowing offence of paragraph (2) (or (4), (6), Article 23(2)) both reach an entity that, knowing it is untrue,
-- tells a donor that it is registered; the reading taken is that both are made out and each carries its own penalty.  F7.5: "or other advantage" is in Article 21(2)(b)(ii) and not in Articles 21(4)(b)(ii),
-- 21(6)(b)(ii) and 23(2)(b)(ii); the reading taken keeps the difference as printed.  F7.8: a term of imprisonment of "2 years" is 24 calendar months (the Penalty provided of domain.l4 stores months).

§ `Part 6 — Use of expressions “Charity”, “charitable” and related terms`

§§ `Nouns of Articles 21 to 23`

-- What a statement says of an entity: the three descriptions the prohibitions are about.
DECLARE `What is said of an entity` IS ONE OF
    `that it is registered by the Commissioner`
    `that it is a “charity”`
    `that it is a “Jersey charity”`

-- The mental elements of the knowing offences, Articles 21(2)(a), 21(4)(a), 21(6)(a) and 23(2)(a): "knows, suspects or has reasonable grounds to suspect".  Each is a fact the caller supplies;
-- "reasonable grounds" is an objective standard the encoding does not compute.
DECLARE `Awareness of a fact under Articles 21 to 23` HAS
    knows IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person knows it
    suspects IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person suspects it
    `reasonable grounds to suspect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person has reasonable grounds to suspect it (an objective standard; the caller decides)

-- What the person making the statement was aware of, about the entity as it is.
DECLARE `Awareness of the person making a statement` HAS
    `that the entity is not a registered charity` IS AN `Awareness of a fact under Articles 21 to 23` @desc Article 21(2)(a)
    `that the entity is a Jersey entity` IS AN `Awareness of a fact under Articles 21 to 23` @desc Article 21(4)(a)(i); the awareness in Article 21(4)(a) is of this and of the entity not being registered, together
    `that the entity is neither a Jersey entity nor an excepted foreign charity` IS AN `Awareness of a fact under Articles 21 to 23` @desc Article 21(6)(a)(i); the awareness in Article 21(6)(a) is of this and of the entity not being registered, together
    `that the entity does not meet all of the conditions of Article 23(3)` IS AN `Awareness of a fact under Articles 21 to 23` @desc Article 23(2)(a)

-- What the person making the statement intended, by so referring to the entity: Articles 21(2)(b), 21(4)(b), 21(6)(b) and 23(2)(b).
DECLARE `Intent of the person making a statement` HAS
    `to cause another person to be misled as to the nature of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Articles 21(2)(b)(i), 21(4)(b)(i), 21(6)(b)(i), 23(2)(b)(i)
    `to cause another person to give the entity any property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Articles 21(2)(b)(ii), 21(4)(b)(ii), 21(6)(b)(ii), 23(2)(b)(ii): property
    `to cause another person to give the entity a financial advantage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Articles 21(2)(b)(ii), 21(4)(b)(ii), 21(6)(b)(ii), 23(2)(b)(ii): financial advantage
    `to cause another person to give the entity some other advantage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc An advantage that is neither property nor financial, for example the time of volunteers; Article 21(2)(b)(ii) says “or other advantage” and Articles 21(4)(b)(ii), 21(6)(b)(ii) and 23(2)(b)(ii) do not (fork F7.5)

-- A statement about an entity, with the facts that decide whether it contravenes a prohibition of Articles 21 and 23.
DECLARE `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` HAS
    `what is said of the entity` IS A `What is said of an entity` @desc What the statement says the entity is
    `in connection with an activity of the entity in Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the statement is made in connection with any of the entity’s activities in Jersey (Articles 21(5) and 21(6))
    `made by the entity itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person making the statement is the entity referring to itself (Articles 21(1)(a), 21(3)(a), 21(5)(a), 23(1)(a) and, by Articles 21(7) and 23(5), the person in Articles 21(2), 21(4), 21(6), 23(2))
    `the entity caused or permitted another person to make it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another person made the statement and the entity caused or permitted that (Articles 21(1)(b), 21(3)(b), 21(5)(b), 23(1)(b))
    `an exception prescribed under Article 21(8) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an exception prescribed by the States by Regulations under Article 21(8) applies to the statement (the content of the Regulations is an input)
    `an exception prescribed under Article 23(4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an exception prescribed by the States by Regulations under Article 23(4) applies to the statement (the content of the Regulations is an input)
    awareness IS AN `Awareness of the person making a statement` @desc What the person making the statement was aware of
    intent IS AN `Intent of the person making a statement` @desc What the person making the statement intended

-- The prohibitions that can be contravened, for the penalty and the offences.
DECLARE `Contravention of Article 21 or Article 23` IS ONE OF
    `paragraph (1) of Article 21`
    `paragraph (2) of Article 21`
    `paragraph (3) of Article 21`
    `paragraph (4) of Article 21`
    `paragraph (5) of Article 21`
    `paragraph (6) of Article 21`
    `paragraph (1) of Article 23`
    `paragraph (2) of Article 23`

-- Who is bound, for the regulative rules.  By Articles 21(7) and 23(5) the knowing offences bind a person whether or not that person is the entity itself.
DECLARE `Party to the prohibitions on expressions` IS ONE OF
    `the entity referred to`
    `a person other than the entity`

-- What is done.  The first is the act of referring to an entity (by the entity, of itself, or by anyone); the second is the entity causing or permitting another person to refer to it.
DECLARE `Act of referring to an entity` IS ONE OF
    `refer to an entity as`
        HAS `what is said` IS A `What is said of an entity`
            `in connection with an activity of the entity in Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN
            `the entity referred to is the speaker` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cause or permit another person to refer to the entity as`
        HAS `what is said` IS A `What is said of an entity`
            `in connection with an activity of the entity in Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Articles 21 and 23 bind or concern an ENTITY: "An entity that is not a registered charity" (21(1), 21(5)), "A Jersey entity" (21(3)), "an entity" that a person refers to (21(2), 21(4), 21(6), 23(2)),
-- "an entity" that does not meet the conditions (23(1)).  A body is an entity only if it falls within a sub-paragraph of Article 2(1): domain.l4's `kinds of entity` is "empty if it is not an entity".
-- A partnership, or a body corporate that is an NPO and falls within none of Article 2(1)(c) to (h) before paragraph (ba) was added on 16 October 2025, is not an entity, and these Articles do not reach it.
-- The guard is applied where the text names an entity: to the subject of 21(1), 21(3), 21(5), 23(1) and to the object of 21(2), 21(4), 21(6), 23(2).  It is NOT applied to "a person" who refers to an entity.
-- src:48 | (1) In this Law, unless the context otherwise requires, “entity” means –
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 2(1); Article 21; Article 23 (src:48), (src:533), (src:578)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The body asked about (integration point IP5); this function reads its field “kinds of entity”
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the body is an entity within Article 2(1)` `the entity` MEANS
    NOT null (`the entity`'s `kinds of entity`)

§§ `Intent and awareness (the limbs the knowing offences share)`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(2)(a), Article 21(4)(a), Article 21(6)(a), Article 23(2)(a) (src:537), (src:545), (src:555), (src:582)
GIVEN fact IS AN `Awareness of a fact under Articles 21 to 23`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person knows, suspects or has reasonable grounds to suspect it` fact MEANS
    fact's knows OR fact's suspects OR fact's `reasonable grounds to suspect`

-- Article 21(2)(b)(ii) says “property or financial or other advantage”, so the helper below is called with TRUE for it (F7.5 does not touch it).
-- Sub-paragraph (b) of each knowing offence: the person intends, by so referring to the entity, to cause another person to be misled as to the nature of the entity, or to give the entity an advantage.
-- Whether the advantage reaches "other advantage" is F7.5; the caller of this helper says which wording applies.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(2)(b), Article 21(4)(b), Article 21(6)(b), Article 23(2)(b) (src:538-540), (src:548-550), (src:558-560), (src:583-585)
GIVEN intent IS AN `Intent of the person making a statement`
      other IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the wording of the sub-paragraph reaches an advantage that is neither property nor financial
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the intent is within the advantage sub-paragraph` intent other MEANS
        intent's `to cause another person to be misled as to the nature of the entity`
    OR  intent's `to cause another person to give the entity any property`
    OR  intent's `to cause another person to give the entity a financial advantage`
    OR  (other AND intent's `to cause another person to give the entity some other advantage`)

-- F7.5: Articles 21(4)(b)(ii), 21(6)(b)(ii) and 23(2)(b)(ii) read “any property or financial advantage”; the reading taken keeps that, the other reading adds “or other advantage”.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(2)(b), Article 21(4)(b), Article 21(6)(b), Article 23(2)(b) (src:538-540), (src:548-550), (src:558-560), (src:583-585)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Articles 21(4)(b)(ii), 21(6)(b)(ii) and 23(2)(b)(ii) reach other advantage under` interp MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `the wording of the advantage limb of the knowing offences`
    WHEN `the wording differs as printed` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the wording is harmonised` THEN TRUE

-- src:532 | 21 Prohibition of unauthorized use of expression “charity” and related terms
§§ `Article 21 — Prohibition of unauthorized use of expression “charity” and related terms`

-- Every paragraph below is split in two.  "The prohibition binds ..." is the standing condition: who is bound, because of what the entity is and, for the knowing offences, what the person knew and intended.
-- "The statement contravenes ..." adds the act: what was said, by whom, and (paragraphs (5) and (6)) in connection with Jersey activities.  The regulative rule uses the first and its act pattern is the second.

-- 21(1) An entity that is not a registered charity (a) must not refer to itself as being registered by the Commissioner; and (b) must not cause or permit another person to refer to the entity as being
-- registered by the Commissioner.  Strict: no mental element.  Contravention is an offence (Article 21(10)): a fine of level 3 on the standard scale.
-- src:533 | (1) An entity that is not a registered charity –
-- src:534 | (a) must not refer to itself as being registered by the Commissioner; and
-- src:535 | (b) must not cause or permit another person to refer to the entity as being registered by the Commissioner.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(1) (src:533)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5); this function reads its field “kinds of entity” (empty: the body is not an entity within Article 2(1), and the paragraph does not reach it) and, in the rules of Article 21(3) to (6), “is a Jersey entity”
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6); the Law’s “registered charity” is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement made about the entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 21(1) the prohibition binds the entity` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement MEANS
        `the body is an entity within Article 2(1)` `the entity`
    AND NOT `the entity is a registered charity`
    AND NOT statement's `an exception prescribed under Article 21(8) applies`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(1)(a) (src:534)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5); this function reads its field “kinds of entity” (empty: the body is not an entity within Article 2(1), and the paragraph does not reach it) and, in the rules of Article 21(3) to (6), “is a Jersey entity”
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement made about the entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 21(1)(a) the entity contravenes sub-paragraph (a)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement MEANS
        `Art 21(1) the prohibition binds the entity` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement
    AND statement's `what is said of the entity` EQUALS `that it is registered by the Commissioner`
    AND statement's `made by the entity itself`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(1)(b) (src:535)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5); this function reads its field “kinds of entity” (empty: the body is not an entity within Article 2(1), and the paragraph does not reach it) and, in the rules of Article 21(3) to (6), “is a Jersey entity”
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement made about the entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 21(1)(b) the entity contravenes sub-paragraph (b)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement MEANS
        `Art 21(1) the prohibition binds the entity` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement
    AND statement's `what is said of the entity` EQUALS `that it is registered by the Commissioner`
    AND statement's `the entity caused or permitted another person to make it`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(1) (src:533-535)
@export Whether a statement contravenes Article 21(1) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: an entity that is not a registered charity refers to itself as being registered by the Commissioner, or causes or permits another person to
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5); this function reads its field “kinds of entity” (empty: the body is not an entity within Article 2(1), and the paragraph does not reach it) and, in the rules of Article 21(3) to (6), “is a Jersey entity”
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement made about the entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 21(1) the statement contravenes paragraph (1)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement MEANS
        `Art 21(1)(a) the entity contravenes sub-paragraph (a)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement
    OR  `Art 21(1)(b) the entity contravenes sub-paragraph (b)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement

-- The regulative rules.  (a) and (b) are separate prohibitions joined by "and"; the paragraph is both.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(1)(a) (src:534)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5); this function reads its field “kinds of entity” (empty: the body is not an entity within Article 2(1), and the paragraph does not reach it) and, in the rules of Article 21(3) to (6), “is a Jersey entity”
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The case: this rule reads only its exception flag; what is said is in the event
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to the prohibitions on expressions` `Act of referring to an entity`
`Art 21(1)(a) an unregistered entity must not refer to itself as being registered by the Commissioner` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement MEANS
    IF   `Art 21(1) the prohibition binds the entity` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement
    THEN PARTY `the entity referred to`
         SHANT `refer to an entity as` `that it is registered by the Commissioner` anywhere TRUE
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the entity referred to` BECAUSE "Article 21(1)(a): an entity that is not a registered charity referred to itself as being registered by the Commissioner"
    ELSE FULFILLED

