      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The case: this rule reads only its exception flag; what is said is in the event
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to the prohibitions on expressions` `Act of referring to an entity`
`Art 21(1)(b) an unregistered entity must not cause or permit another person to refer to it as being registered by the Commissioner` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement MEANS
    IF   `Art 21(1) the prohibition binds the entity` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement
    THEN PARTY `the entity referred to`
         SHANT `cause or permit another person to refer to the entity as` `that it is registered by the Commissioner` anywhere
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the entity referred to` BECAUSE "Article 21(1)(b): an entity that is not a registered charity caused or permitted another person to refer to it as being registered by the Commissioner"
