@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(1) (src:533-535)
@export The prohibition of Article 21(1) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 as a rule: an entity that is not a registered charity must not refer to itself as being registered by the Commissioner, nor cause or permit another person to
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5); this function reads its field “kinds of entity” (empty: the body is not an entity within Article 2(1), and the paragraph does not reach it) and, in the rules of Article 21(3) to (6), “is a Jersey entity”
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The case: this rule reads only its exception flag; what is said is in the event
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to the prohibitions on expressions` `Act of referring to an entity`
`Art 21(1) an unregistered entity must not say it is registered by the Commissioner` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement MEANS
        `Art 21(1)(a) an unregistered entity must not refer to itself as being registered by the Commissioner` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement
    RAND `Art 21(1)(b) an unregistered entity must not cause or permit another person to refer to it as being registered by the Commissioner` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement

-- 21(7) Paragraphs (2), (4) and (6) apply whether or not the person making the reference is also the entity, and is referring to itself.  The paragraphs apply either way, so the answer is TRUE for both values of the input.
-- src:561 | (7) Paragraphs (2), (4) and (6) apply whether or not the person making the reference is also the entity, and is referring to itself.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(7) (src:561)
GIVEN `the person making the reference is the entity referring to itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person making the reference is the entity itself
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 21(7) paragraphs (2), (4) and (6) apply to the person making the reference` `the person making the reference is the entity referring to itself` MEANS
    TRUE

-- 21(2) A person must not refer to an entity, that is not a registered charity, as being registered by the Commissioner, if the person (a) knows, suspects or has reasonable grounds to suspect that the entity
-- is not a registered charity; and (b) intends, by so referring to the entity, to cause another person (i) to be misled as to the nature of the entity, or (ii) to give to the entity any property or financial or other advantage.
-- Contravention is an offence (Article 21(9)): imprisonment for a term of 2 years and a fine.
-- src:536 | (2) A person must not refer to an entity, that is not a registered charity, as being registered by the Commissioner, if the person –
-- src:537 | (a) knows, suspects or has reasonable grounds to suspect that the entity is not a registered charity; and
-- src:538 | (b) intends, by so referring to the entity, to cause another person –
-- src:539 | (i) to be misled as to the nature of the entity, or
-- src:540 | (ii) to give to the entity any property or financial or other advantage.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(2) (src:536-540)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5); this function reads its field “kinds of entity” (empty: the body is not an entity within Article 2(1), and the paragraph does not reach it) and, in the rules of Article 21(3) to (6), “is a Jersey entity”
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement made about the entity, with the awareness and the intent of the person making it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 21(2) the prohibition binds the person` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement MEANS
        `the body is an entity within Article 2(1)` `the entity`
    AND NOT `the entity is a registered charity`
    AND `Art 21(7) paragraphs (2), (4) and (6) apply to the person making the reference` (statement's `made by the entity itself`)
    AND `the person knows, suspects or has reasonable grounds to suspect it` (statement's awareness's `that the entity is not a registered charity`)
    AND `the intent is within the advantage sub-paragraph` (statement's intent) TRUE
    AND NOT statement's `an exception prescribed under Article 21(8) applies`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(2) (src:536-540)
@export Whether a statement contravenes Article 21(2) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: a person refers to an unregistered entity as being registered by the Commissioner, knowing, suspecting or having reasonable grounds to suspect that it is not, and intending to mislead as to its nature or to obtain property or a financial or other advantage for it
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5); this function reads its field “kinds of entity” (empty: the body is not an entity within Article 2(1), and the paragraph does not reach it) and, in the rules of Article 21(3) to (6), “is a Jersey entity”
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement made about the entity, with the awareness and the intent of the person making it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 21(2) the statement contravenes paragraph (2)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement MEANS
        `Art 21(2) the prohibition binds the person` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement
    AND statement's `what is said of the entity` EQUALS `that it is registered by the Commissioner`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(2) (src:536-540)
@export The prohibition of Article 21(2) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 as a rule: a person (the entity itself, by Article 21(7), or anyone else) must not refer to an unregistered entity as being registered by the Commissioner when the person knows, suspects or has reasonable grounds to suspect that it is not and intends to mislead or to obtain an advantage
GIVEN referrer IS A `Party to the prohibitions on expressions` @desc Who makes the reference: the entity itself or a person other than the entity (Article 21(7): the paragraph binds either)
      `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5); this function reads its field “kinds of entity” (empty: the body is not an entity within Article 2(1), and the paragraph does not reach it) and, in the rules of Article 21(3) to (6), “is a Jersey entity”
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The case: the awareness and the intent of the person making the reference, and the exception flag; what is said is in the event
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to the prohibitions on expressions` `Act of referring to an entity`
`Art 21(2) a person must not say that an unregistered entity is registered, with knowledge and intent` referrer `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement MEANS
    IF   `Art 21(2) the prohibition binds the person` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement
    THEN PARTY referrer
         SHANT `refer to an entity as` `that it is registered by the Commissioner` anywhere itself
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY referrer BECAUSE "Article 21(2): a person referred to an entity that is not a registered charity as being registered by the Commissioner, knowing or suspecting that it is not, and intending to mislead or to obtain an advantage"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 21(3) A Jersey entity that is not a registered charity (a) must not refer to itself as a “charity”; and (b) must not cause or permit another person to refer to the entity as a “charity”.  Strict.
-- Contravention is an offence (Article 21(10)).  A body that is both a Jersey entity and (as the United Kingdom body extended to Jersey of trap T25) an excepted foreign charity is caught here:
-- the excepted foreign charity is an exception only to paragraphs (5) and (6).
-- src:541 | (3) A Jersey entity that is not a registered charity –
-- src:542 | (a) must not refer to itself as a “charity”; and
-- src:543 | (b) must not cause or permit another person to refer to the entity as a “charity”.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(3) (src:541)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5); this function reads its field “is a Jersey entity”
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement made about the entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 21(3) the prohibition binds the Jersey entity` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement MEANS
        `the body is an entity within Article 2(1)` `the entity`
    AND `the entity`'s `is a Jersey entity`
    AND NOT `the entity is a registered charity`
    AND NOT statement's `an exception prescribed under Article 21(8) applies`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(3)(a) (src:542)
