-- 21(8) The States may by Regulations prescribe exceptions to the prohibitions in paragraphs (1) to (6).  A power of the States, typed MAY; the Regulations are not among the sources, and whether an
-- exception applies to a statement is the input `an exception prescribed under Article 21(8) applies` above.
-- src:562 | (8) The States may by Regulations prescribe exceptions to the prohibitions in paragraphs (1) to (6).

-- The powers that Part 6 gives to the States and to the Minister, by what is done (the content of the Regulations and of the Orders is an input).
DECLARE `Power exercised under Articles 21 to 23` IS ONE OF
    `prescribe by Regulations exceptions to the prohibitions in Article 21(1) to (6)`
    `prescribe by Order a jurisdiction whose law establishes an excepted foreign charity`
    `prescribe by Order that a specified entity is not required to meet the first condition of an excepted foreign charity`
    `amend by Regulations the conditions of an excepted foreign charity`
    `prescribe by Regulations exceptions to the prohibitions in Article 23(1) and (2)`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(8) (src:562)
@export The power of the States by Regulations to prescribe exceptions to the prohibitions in Article 21(1) to (6) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, as a rule: the States may; the content of the Regulations is an input
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Power exercised under Articles 21 to 23`
`Art 21(8) the States may prescribe exceptions` MEANS
    PARTY `the States`
    MAY `prescribe by Regulations exceptions to the prohibitions in Article 21(1) to (6)`

-- 21(9) An entity or other person, that contravenes paragraph (2), (4) or (6), commits an offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of 2 years and to a fine.
-- 21(10) An entity, that contravenes paragraph (1), (3) or (5), commits an offence and is liable to a fine of level 3 on the standard scale.
-- The penalty is DATA: a term of imprisonment is a maximum, stored in months (domain.l4), and the fine is "a fine" with no maximum stated, or "a fine of level 3 on the standard scale", whose amount is in
-- the Criminal Justice (Standard Scale of Fines) (Jersey) Law, which is not among the sources and is not invented here.
-- src:563 | (9) An entity or other person, that contravenes paragraph (2), (4) or (6), commits an offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of 2 years and to a fine.
-- src:564 | (10) An entity, that contravenes paragraph (1), (3) or (5), commits an offence and is liable to a fine of level 3 on the standard scale.

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(9), Article 23(7) (src:563)
GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`the penalty of imprisonment for a term of 2 years and a fine` MEANS
    `Penalty provided` WITH
        `imprisonment up to, in months` IS JUST 24
        fine IS `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(10), Article 23(6) (src:564)
GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`the penalty of a fine of level 3 on the standard scale` MEANS
    `Penalty provided` WITH
        `imprisonment up to, in months` IS NOTHING
        fine IS `a fine of a level on the standard scale` 3

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(9) and (10), Article 23(6) and (7) (src:563-564), (src:592-593)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this is not a paragraph of the Article asked about` MEANS
    REFUSE "this is not a paragraph of the Article asked about: Article 21 has the offences of paragraphs (9) and (10) for paragraphs (1) to (6), and Article 23 has paragraphs (6) and (7) for paragraphs (1) and (2)"

-- The penalty for any of the eight prohibitions: one function from the paragraph contravened to the penalty as data (integration point IP30, consumed by Article 37(1)).
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(9) and (10), Article 23(6) and (7) (src:563-564), (src:592-593)
@export The penalty that Articles 21 and 23 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 provide for contravening a given paragraph: paragraphs 21(1), 21(3), 21(5) and 23(1) a fine of level 3 on the standard scale; paragraphs 21(2), 21(4), 21(6) and 23(2) imprisonment for a term of 2 years (24 months) and a fine with no maximum stated
GIVEN contravention IS A `Contravention of Article 21 or Article 23` @desc The paragraph of Article 21 or Article 23 contravened
GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` contravention MEANS
    CONSIDER contravention
    WHEN `paragraph (1) of Article 21` THEN `the penalty of a fine of level 3 on the standard scale`
    WHEN `paragraph (2) of Article 21` THEN `the penalty of imprisonment for a term of 2 years and a fine`
    WHEN `paragraph (3) of Article 21` THEN `the penalty of a fine of level 3 on the standard scale`
    WHEN `paragraph (4) of Article 21` THEN `the penalty of imprisonment for a term of 2 years and a fine`
    WHEN `paragraph (5) of Article 21` THEN `the penalty of a fine of level 3 on the standard scale`
    WHEN `paragraph (6) of Article 21` THEN `the penalty of imprisonment for a term of 2 years and a fine`
    WHEN `paragraph (1) of Article 23` THEN `the penalty of a fine of level 3 on the standard scale`
    WHEN `paragraph (2) of Article 23` THEN `the penalty of imprisonment for a term of 2 years and a fine`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(9) and (10) (src:563-564)
@export The penalty that Article 21 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 provides for contravening a given paragraph (a refusal for a paragraph of Article 23)
GIVEN contravention IS A `Contravention of Article 21 or Article 23` @desc The paragraph of Article 21 contravened
GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`Art 21 the penalty for the contravention` contravention MEANS
    CONSIDER contravention
    WHEN `paragraph (1) of Article 21` THEN `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` contravention
    WHEN `paragraph (2) of Article 21` THEN `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` contravention
    WHEN `paragraph (3) of Article 21` THEN `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` contravention
    WHEN `paragraph (4) of Article 21` THEN `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` contravention
    WHEN `paragraph (5) of Article 21` THEN `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` contravention
    WHEN `paragraph (6) of Article 21` THEN `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` contravention
    WHEN `paragraph (1) of Article 23` THEN `this is not a paragraph of the Article asked about`
    WHEN `paragraph (2) of Article 23` THEN `this is not a paragraph of the Article asked about`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(9) (src:563)
@export Whether a statement is an offence under Article 21(9) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: the person contravenes paragraph (2), (4) or (6) (imprisonment for a term of 2 years and a fine)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5)
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      `the entity is an excepted foreign charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is an excepted foreign charity (integration point IP26)
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement made about the entity
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.5
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 21(9) the statement is an offence under paragraph (9)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is an excepted foreign charity` statement interp MEANS
        `Art 21(2) the statement contravenes paragraph (2)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement
    OR  `Art 21(4) the statement contravenes paragraph (4)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement interp
    OR  `Art 21(6) the statement contravenes paragraph (6)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is an excepted foreign charity` statement interp

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(10) (src:564)
@export Whether a statement is an offence under Article 21(10) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: the entity contravenes paragraph (1), (3) or (5) (a fine of level 3 on the standard scale)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5)
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      `the entity is an excepted foreign charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is an excepted foreign charity (integration point IP26)
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement made about the entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 21(10) the statement is an offence under paragraph (10)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is an excepted foreign charity` statement MEANS
        `Art 21(1) the statement contravenes paragraph (1)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement
    OR  `Art 21(3) the statement contravenes paragraph (3)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement
    OR  `Art 21(5) the statement contravenes paragraph (5)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is an excepted foreign charity` statement

-- src:565 | 22 Excepted foreign charities
§§ `Article 22 — Excepted foreign charities`

-- src:566 | (1) For the purpose of Article 21, an entity is an excepted foreign charity if it meets both the condition in paragraph (2) and the condition in paragraph (3).

-- Under whose law the entity is established, for the first condition of Article 22(2)(a).  Whether a jurisdiction is “prescribed” is an input (the Order under 22(2)(a)(ii) is not among the sources).
DECLARE `Law under which an entity is established` IS ONE OF
    `the law of the United Kingdom or of a jurisdiction that is part of the United Kingdom`
    `the law of a jurisdiction, not Jersey or the United Kingdom or a part of it, that the Minister has prescribed by Order under Article 22(2)(a)(ii)`
    `the law of Jersey`
    `the law of some other jurisdiction`

-- The facts Article 22 asks about the entity (the registered-charity fact is the standard input of IP6, not a field here).
DECLARE `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` HAS
    `established under` IS A `Law under which an entity is established` @desc The law under which the entity is established
    `entitled under that law to refer to itself there as a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 22(2)(b): entitled, under the law of that jurisdiction, to refer to itself in that jurisdiction as a “charity” (or by any equivalent term in a language other than English that is used there)
    `managed wholly or mainly from that jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 22(3)(a): managed wholly or mainly from the jurisdiction under the law of which it is established
    `specified in an Order under Article 22(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a specified-entity Order under Article 22(4) says that this entity is not required to meet the first condition (the content of the Order is an input)

-- 22(2) The first condition is that the entity is (a) established under the law (i) of the United Kingdom, or of any jurisdiction that is part of the United Kingdom, or (ii) of a jurisdiction (not being Jersey,
-- the United Kingdom or a part of the United Kingdom) that is prescribed for this purpose by the Minister by Order; and (b) entitled, under the law of that jurisdiction, to refer to itself in that jurisdiction as a
-- “charity” (or by any equivalent term in a language other than English that is used in that jurisdiction).
-- src:567 | (2) The first condition is that the entity is –
-- src:568 | (a) established under the law –
-- src:569 | (i) of the United Kingdom, or of any jurisdiction that is part of the United Kingdom, or
-- src:570 | (ii) of a jurisdiction (not being Jersey, the United Kingdom or a part of the United Kingdom) that is prescribed for this purpose by the Minister by Order; and
-- src:571 | (b) entitled, under the law of that jurisdiction, to refer to itself in that jurisdiction as a “charity” (or by any equivalent term in a language other than English that is used in that jurisdiction).
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 22(2)(a) (src:568-570)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` @desc The facts about the entity that Article 22 asks about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 22(2)(a) the entity is established under the law of the United Kingdom or of a prescribed jurisdiction` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `established under`
    WHEN `the law of the United Kingdom or of a jurisdiction that is part of the United Kingdom` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the law of a jurisdiction, not Jersey or the United Kingdom or a part of it, that the Minister has prescribed by Order under Article 22(2)(a)(ii)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the law of Jersey` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the law of some other jurisdiction` THEN FALSE

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 22(2) (src:567-571)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` @desc The facts about the entity that Article 22 asks about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 22(2) the entity meets the first condition` facts MEANS
        `Art 22(2)(a) the entity is established under the law of the United Kingdom or of a prescribed jurisdiction` facts
    AND facts's `entitled under that law to refer to itself there as a charity`

-- 22(3) The second condition is that the entity (a) is managed wholly or mainly from the jurisdiction under the law of which it is established; and (b) is not a registered charity.
-- (Paragraph (b) repeats the opening words of Article 21(5) and (6): trap T25, kept as the Law has it.)
-- src:572 | (3) The second condition is that the entity –
-- src:573 | (a) is managed wholly or mainly from the jurisdiction under the law of which it is established; and
-- src:574 | (b) is not a registered charity.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 22(3) (src:572-574)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` @desc The facts about the entity that Article 22 asks about
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 22(3) the entity meets the second condition` facts `the entity is a registered charity` MEANS
        facts's `managed wholly or mainly from that jurisdiction`
    AND NOT `the entity is a registered charity`

-- 22(4) The Minister may by Order prescribe that a specified entity is not required to meet the first condition, despite sub-paragraphs (a) and (b) of paragraph (2).
-- src:575 | (4) The Minister may by Order prescribe that a specified entity is not required to meet the first condition, despite sub-paragraphs (a) and (b) of paragraph (2).
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 22(4) (src:575)
@export The power of the Minister by Order to prescribe that a specified entity is not required to meet the first condition of an excepted foreign charity (Article 22(4) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014), as a rule: the Minister may; the Order is an input
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Power exercised under Articles 21 to 23`
`Art 22(4) the Minister may exempt a specified entity from the first condition` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `prescribe by Order that a specified entity is not required to meet the first condition of an excepted foreign charity`

-- 22(2)(a)(ii) A jurisdiction “prescribed for this purpose by the Minister by Order”: a power of the Minister, typed MAY.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 22(2)(a)(ii) (src:570)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Power exercised under Articles 21 to 23`
`Art 22(2)(a)(ii) the Minister may prescribe a jurisdiction by Order` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `prescribe by Order a jurisdiction whose law establishes an excepted foreign charity`

-- 22(5) The States may by Regulations amend paragraph (1), (2) or (3) to make different provision as to the conditions that are to be met.  A power of the States; it can change the answer of this Article,
-- and the Regulations are not among the sources (an amendment would be a new vintage, not an input to this rule).
-- src:576 | (5) The States may by Regulations amend paragraph (1), (2) or (3) to make different provision as to the conditions that are to be met.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 22(5) (src:576)
@export The power of the States by Regulations to amend the conditions of an excepted foreign charity (Article 22(5) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014), as a rule: the States may; the Regulations are not in the sources
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Power exercised under Articles 21 to 23`
`Art 22(5) the States may amend the conditions` MEANS
    PARTY `the States`
    MAY `amend by Regulations the conditions of an excepted foreign charity`

-- 22(1) For the purpose of Article 21, an entity is an excepted foreign charity if it meets both the condition in paragraph (2) and the condition in paragraph (3).  An entity specified under paragraph (4) is not
-- required to meet the first condition.  The answer is integration point IP26: the Jersey entity of Article 2(3) is outside it only by Article 21(3) and (4) (a body that is both is caught there, trap T25).
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 22(1) and (4) (src:566), (src:575)
@export Whether an entity is an excepted foreign charity for the purpose of Article 21 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: it meets the first condition (established under UK law or the law of a prescribed jurisdiction, and entitled there to call itself a charity) unless an Order under Article 22(4) says it need not, and the second (managed from that jurisdiction, and not a registered charity)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` @desc The facts about the entity that Article 22 asks about
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` facts `the entity is a registered charity` MEANS
        (`Art 22(2) the entity meets the first condition` facts OR facts's `specified in an Order under Article 22(4)`)
    AND `Art 22(3) the entity meets the second condition` facts `the entity is a registered charity`

-- F7.12.  Article 22(1) defines an excepted foreign charity “For the purpose of Article 21”.  Article 2(10)(b) (misconduct: an offence in relation to a registered charity or to an excepted foreign charity)
-- says “an excepted foreign charity (within the meaning of Article 22)”, and 22(1) does not reach that Article.  Reading taken: Article 22 defines the term wherever the Law uses it, so the answer is the one above.
-- The other reading: the definition is for Article 21 only, so Article 2(10)(b) has no definition of the term to apply and the question is refused.  (Article 22 is also in force only from 1 January 2019, trap T30.)
-- src:111 | (b) the commission by any person, in relation a registered charity or to an excepted foreign charity (within the meaning of Article 22) or to an entity equivalent to a registered charity under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey, of an offence –
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 2(10)(b), Article 22(1) (src:111), (src:566)
@export Whether an entity is an excepted foreign charity for the purpose of Article 2(10)(b) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, on the reading chosen at F7.12: by default Article 22 defines the term wherever the Law uses it; on the other reading Article 22 defines it for Article 21 only and the answer is a refusal
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` @desc The facts about the entity that Article 22 asks about
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.12
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity for the purpose of Article 2(10)(b)` facts `the entity is a registered charity` interp MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `whether Article 22 defines an excepted foreign charity outside Article 21`
    WHEN `Article 22 defines the term wherever the Law uses it` THEN `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` facts `the entity is a registered charity`
    WHEN `Article 22 defines the term for Article 21 only` THEN `Article 22 defines the term for Article 21 only, so it does not define it for Article 2(10)(b)`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 22(1), Article 2(10)(b) (src:566), (src:111)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 22 defines the term for Article 21 only, so it does not define it for Article 2(10)(b)` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 22(1) defines an excepted foreign charity “for the purpose of Article 21” only, so on this reading Article 2(10)(b), which cites Article 22, has no definition of the term to apply"

-- src:577 | 23 Prohibition of unauthorized use of expression “Jersey charity”
§§ `Article 23 — Prohibition of unauthorized use of expression “Jersey charity”`

-- 23(3) The conditions are that the entity (a) is a registered charity; (b) is a Jersey entity; and (c) is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey.
-- src:586 | (3) The conditions are that the entity –
-- src:587 | (a) is a registered charity;
-- src:588 | (b) is a Jersey entity; and
-- src:589 | (c) is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 23(3) (src:586-589)
@export Whether an entity meets all of the conditions of Article 23(3) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 for being called a “Jersey charity”: it is a registered charity, a Jersey entity, and wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5); this function reads its field “is a Jersey entity”
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 23(3)(c); a fact the caller supplies
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 23(3) the entity meets all of the conditions` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` MEANS
        "(a)" ... `the entity is a registered charity`
    AND "(b)" ... `the entity`'s `is a Jersey entity`
    AND "(c)" ... `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey`

-- 23(5) Paragraph (2) applies whether or not the person making the reference is also the entity, and is referring to itself.
-- src:591 | (5) Paragraph (2) applies whether or not the person making the reference is also the entity, and is referring to itself.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 23(5) (src:591)
GIVEN `the person making the reference is the entity referring to itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person making the reference is the entity itself
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 23(5) paragraph (2) applies to the person making the reference` `the person making the reference is the entity referring to itself` MEANS
    TRUE

-- 23(1) Unless an entity meets all of the conditions in paragraph (3), that entity (a) must not refer to itself as a “Jersey charity”; and (b) must not cause or permit another person to refer to the entity as a
-- “Jersey charity”.  Strict.  Offence: Article 23(6), a fine of level 3 on the standard scale.  Paragraphs (1) and (2) are subject to any exception prescribed by the States by Regulations (23(4)).
-- src:578 | (1) Unless an entity meets all of the conditions in paragraph (3), that entity –
-- src:579 | (a) must not refer to itself as a “Jersey charity”; and
-- src:580 | (b) must not cause or permit another person to refer to the entity as a “Jersey charity”.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 23(1) (src:578)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5)
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 23(3)(c); a fact the caller supplies
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement made about the entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 23(1) the prohibition binds the entity` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` statement MEANS
        `the body is an entity within Article 2(1)` `the entity`
    AND NOT `Art 23(3) the entity meets all of the conditions` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey`
    AND NOT statement's `an exception prescribed under Article 23(4) applies`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 23(1)(a) (src:579)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5)
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 23(3)(c); a fact the caller supplies
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement made about the entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 23(1)(a) the entity contravenes sub-paragraph (a)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` statement MEANS
        `Art 23(1) the prohibition binds the entity` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` statement
    AND statement's `what is said of the entity` EQUALS `that it is a “Jersey charity”`
    AND statement's `made by the entity itself`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 23(1)(b) (src:580)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5)
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 23(3)(c); a fact the caller supplies
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement made about the entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 23(1)(b) the entity contravenes sub-paragraph (b)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` statement MEANS
        `Art 23(1) the prohibition binds the entity` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` statement
    AND statement's `what is said of the entity` EQUALS `that it is a “Jersey charity”`
    AND statement's `the entity caused or permitted another person to make it`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 23(1) (src:578-580)
@export Whether a statement contravenes Article 23(1) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: an entity that does not meet all of the conditions of Article 23(3) refers to itself as a “Jersey charity”, or causes or permits another person to
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5); this function reads its field “is a Jersey entity”
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 23(3)(c); a fact the caller supplies
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement made about the entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 23(1) the statement contravenes paragraph (1)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` statement MEANS
        `Art 23(1)(a) the entity contravenes sub-paragraph (a)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` statement
    OR  `Art 23(1)(b) the entity contravenes sub-paragraph (b)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` statement

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 23(1)(a) (src:579)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5)
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 23(3)(c); a fact the caller supplies
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The case: this rule reads only its exception flag; what is said is in the event
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to the prohibitions on expressions` `Act of referring to an entity`
`Art 23(1)(a) an entity must not refer to itself as a “Jersey charity” unless it meets the conditions` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` statement MEANS
    IF   `Art 23(1) the prohibition binds the entity` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` statement
    THEN PARTY `the entity referred to`
         SHANT `refer to an entity as` `that it is a “Jersey charity”` anywhere TRUE
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the entity referred to` BECAUSE "Article 23(1)(a): an entity that does not meet all of the conditions of Article 23(3) referred to itself as a “Jersey charity”"
    ELSE FULFILLED

