@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 23(6) and (7) (src:592-593)
@export The penalty that Article 23 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 provides for contravening a given paragraph (a refusal for a paragraph of Article 21)
GIVEN contravention IS A `Contravention of Article 21 or Article 23` @desc The paragraph of Article 23 contravened
GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`Art 23 the penalty for the contravention` contravention MEANS
    CONSIDER contravention
    WHEN `paragraph (1) of Article 21` THEN `this is not a paragraph of the Article asked about`
    WHEN `paragraph (2) of Article 21` THEN `this is not a paragraph of the Article asked about`
    WHEN `paragraph (3) of Article 21` THEN `this is not a paragraph of the Article asked about`
    WHEN `paragraph (4) of Article 21` THEN `this is not a paragraph of the Article asked about`
    WHEN `paragraph (5) of Article 21` THEN `this is not a paragraph of the Article asked about`
    WHEN `paragraph (6) of Article 21` THEN `this is not a paragraph of the Article asked about`
    WHEN `paragraph (1) of Article 23` THEN `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` contravention
    WHEN `paragraph (2) of Article 23` THEN `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` contravention

§§ `One statement, several contraventions (fork F7.4) and the length of a term (fork F7.8)`

-- F7.4.  An unregistered entity that tells a donor, knowing it to be untrue, that it is registered with the Commissioner contravenes both paragraph (1)(a), which is strict, and paragraph (2), which Article 21(7)
-- extends to the entity itself.  Reading taken: both contraventions are made out and each has its own penalty.  Other reading: the knowing offence displaces the strict one.  The same question arises in the pairs
-- (3) and (4), (5) and (6), and Article 23(1) and (2).
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Articles 21(1) to (10) and 23(1) to (7) (src:533-564), (src:578-593)
@export The contraventions of Articles 21 and 23 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 that one statement makes out, in the order of the paragraphs; on the reading taken at F7.4 a strict contravention and the knowing contravention of its pair are both listed
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5)
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      `the entity is an excepted foreign charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is an excepted foreign charity (integration point IP26)
      `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 23(3)(c); a fact the caller supplies
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement made about the entity, with the awareness and the intent of the person making it
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.4 and F7.5
GIVETH A LIST OF `Contravention of Article 21 or Article 23`
`Art 21 and 23: the contraventions made out by the statement` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is an excepted foreign charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` statement interp MEANS
    filter made
           (LIST `paragraph (1) of Article 21`, `paragraph (2) of Article 21`, `paragraph (3) of Article 21`, `paragraph (4) of Article 21`,
                 `paragraph (5) of Article 21`, `paragraph (6) of Article 21`, `paragraph (1) of Article 23`, `paragraph (2) of Article 23`)
    WHERE
        displaces MEANS
            CONSIDER interp's `how the strict and the knowing offences combine for one act`
            WHEN `both offences are made out` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `the knowing offence displaces the strict one` THEN TRUE
        made contravention MEANS
            CONSIDER contravention
            WHEN `paragraph (1) of Article 21` THEN
                `Art 21(1) the statement contravenes paragraph (1)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement
                AND NOT (displaces AND `Art 21(2) the statement contravenes paragraph (2)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement)
            WHEN `paragraph (2) of Article 21` THEN `Art 21(2) the statement contravenes paragraph (2)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement
            WHEN `paragraph (3) of Article 21` THEN
                `Art 21(3) the statement contravenes paragraph (3)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement
                AND NOT (displaces AND `Art 21(4) the statement contravenes paragraph (4)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement interp)
            WHEN `paragraph (4) of Article 21` THEN `Art 21(4) the statement contravenes paragraph (4)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` statement interp
            WHEN `paragraph (5) of Article 21` THEN
                `Art 21(5) the statement contravenes paragraph (5)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is an excepted foreign charity` statement
                AND NOT (displaces AND `Art 21(6) the statement contravenes paragraph (6)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is an excepted foreign charity` statement interp)
            WHEN `paragraph (6) of Article 21` THEN `Art 21(6) the statement contravenes paragraph (6)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is an excepted foreign charity` statement interp
            WHEN `paragraph (1) of Article 23` THEN
                `Art 23(1) the statement contravenes paragraph (1)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` statement
                AND NOT (displaces AND `Art 23(2) the statement contravenes paragraph (2)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` statement interp)
            WHEN `paragraph (2) of Article 23` THEN `Art 23(2) the statement contravenes paragraph (2)` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` statement interp

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Articles 21(1) to (10) and 23(1) to (7) (src:533-564), (src:578-593)
@export The penalties that Articles 21 and 23 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 provide for one statement, one for each contravention it makes out, in the order of the paragraphs
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity (integration point IP5)
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a registered charity (integration point IP6)
      `the entity is an excepted foreign charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is an excepted foreign charity (integration point IP26)
      `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 23(3)(c); a fact the caller supplies
      statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement made about the entity, with the awareness and the intent of the person making it
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.4 and F7.5
GIVETH A LIST OF `Penalty provided`
`Art 21 and 23: the penalties for the statement` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is an excepted foreign charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` statement interp MEANS
    map (GIVEN contravention YIELD `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` contravention)
        (`Art 21 and 23: the contraventions made out by the statement` `the entity` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity is an excepted foreign charity` `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` statement interp)

-- F7.8.  “imprisonment for a term of 2 years” (Articles 21(9) and 23(7)): the unit of the term.  Reading taken: 2 calendar years, counted by adding 24 months to the day the term begins
-- (clamping at the end of a month).  Other reading: 730 days.  The Penalty provided of domain.l4 stores 24 months on either reading; the unit matters when a sentence is measured in days.
-- A sentence is a MAXIMUM here: “liable to imprisonment for a term of 2 years”, so a shorter sentence is within it.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(9), Article 23(7) (src:563), (src:593)
@export The day on which a term of imprisonment of 2 years (Articles 21(9) and 23(7) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014) that begins on a given day ends, by the unit chosen at F7.8 (default: 24 calendar months)
GIVEN start IS A DATE @desc The day the term begins
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.8
GIVETH A DATE
`Art 21(9) and 23(7) the day on which a term of imprisonment of 2 years beginning on a day ends` start interp MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `the unit of a term of imprisonment`
    WHEN `calendar months` THEN `add months` start 24
    WHEN `days` THEN Date (Day start PLUS 730)

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 21(9), Article 23(7) (src:563), (src:593)
@export Whether a sentence of a given number of days, beginning on a given day, is within the maximum of 2 years of Articles 21(9) and 23(7) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, by the unit chosen at F7.8
GIVEN days IS A NUMBER @desc The length of the sentence in days
      start IS A DATE @desc The day the sentence begins
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.8
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` days start interp MEANS
    days AT MOST (Day (`Art 21(9) and 23(7) the day on which a term of imprisonment of 2 years beginning on a day ends` start interp) MINUS Day start)
